WEBVTT

00:07.553 --> 00:12.217
As our trajectory continues, the massive body

00:12.277 --> 00:15.159
of the parent planet moves directly between us

00:15.519 --> 00:20.503
and the sun. We are now entering the penumbra,

00:22.364 --> 00:27.208
the outer edge of the celestial shadow. The

00:27.248 --> 00:30.791
temperature will begin to drop rapidly as the

00:30.871 --> 00:37.659
light is obscured. Solar efficiency will fall

00:37.739 --> 00:43.681
to critical levels. Prepare for deep space

00:43.821 --> 00:49.684
isolation as we cross the threshold into total

00:49.804 --> 00:50.444
darkness.

01:25.965 --> 01:29.569
They clear the dark and cut the heavy lines

01:29.769 --> 01:33.793
Leaving all the medical machinery behind I'm

01:33.853 --> 01:37.657
sitting in the co-pilot seat in the dark

01:38.157 --> 01:42.261
Watching my anchor try to pilot the spark But the

01:42.782 --> 01:47.066
edge of the planet is cutting the light A massive

01:47.166 --> 01:50.568
eclipse in the middle of the night I see the

01:50.628 --> 01:54.610
temperature drop on the console screen The

01:54.690 --> 01:59.533
coldest shadow that we've ever seen Entering

01:59.553 --> 02:04.355
the shadow, crossing the line Losing the light,

02:04.636 --> 02:09.638
losing the sign The power is draining, the cabin

02:09.738 --> 02:13.300
is dark But I'm not alone, in the middle of the

02:13.320 --> 02:17.764
dark We're caught in the penumbra, cold and

02:17.824 --> 02:22.827
blind Leaving the warmth of the sun behind But

02:22.887 --> 02:26.650
the engine is running and the heavy guitars play

02:26.971 --> 02:30.173
We're pushing through the shadow to the light of

02:30.253 --> 02:34.596
day I lost my legs but I didn't lose the fight

02:34.836 --> 02:38.179
We're riding through the center of the endless

02:38.299 --> 02:41.441
night Transit through the penumbra

02:48.973 --> 02:53.376
The machinery hums with a desperate sound A

02:53.496 --> 02:58.159
million miles from the solid ground I look at the

02:58.239 --> 03:02.963
crew in the freezing air The freight dogs and the

03:03.063 --> 03:06.865
captain sitting right there The solar arrays

03:07.065 --> 03:12.129
are starting to freeze A sudden drop by a hundred

03:12.189 --> 03:15.651
degrees But the structural integrity is

03:15.731 --> 03:19.414
holding the line I've got the family here and the

03:19.474 --> 03:23.297
telemetry is fine Entering the shadow,

03:23.537 --> 03:28.661
crossing the line Losing the light, losing the

03:28.801 --> 03:33.605
sign The power is draining, the cabin is dark But

03:33.885 --> 03:37.548
I'm not alone in the middle of the dark We're

03:37.648 --> 03:42.170
caught in the penumbra, cold and blind Leaving

03:42.190 --> 03:46.651
the warmth of the sun behind But the engine is

03:46.731 --> 03:50.052
running and the heavy guitars play We're

03:50.112 --> 03:54.233
pushing through the shadow to the light of day I

03:54.274 --> 03:57.735
lost my legs but I didn't lose the fight We're

03:57.795 --> 04:01.556
riding through the center of the endless night

04:02.036 --> 04:04.437
Transit through the penumbra

04:35.724 --> 04:41.027
Just a phase of the orbit. Just a test of the

04:41.127 --> 04:49.721
steel. The shadow is heavy. But the anchor holds

04:49.801 --> 04:54.803
the wheel We're caught in the penumbra cold and

04:55.083 --> 05:00.005
blind Leaving the warmth of the sun behind But

05:00.085 --> 05:03.787
the engine is running and the heavy guitars play

05:04.107 --> 05:07.308
We're pushing through the shadow to the light of

05:07.348 --> 05:11.730
day I lost my legs but I didn't lose the fight

05:11.930 --> 05:15.272
We're riding through the center of the endless

05:15.412 --> 05:18.996
night transit through the penumbra

05:21.360 --> 05:26.908
wait for the dawn we're making the transit

05:29.432 --> 05:30.854
through the penumbra

